A||N||3||beachbomb||Where is the VSS?||||5||
Z||000000||beachbomb||11-27-2000||04:59 PM||||Hi all, i'm trying to find the vehicle speed sensor on my '84 4 cyclinder, any idea where it is?, thanks..jim('84 Indy)||||reg||5
Z||000001||deceler8||11-27-2000||05:16 PM||||It's that thing you bump with your oil filter when you change oil...it's right down in the oil filter area and attached to the transaxle towards the passenger side. Has a wire harness coming out of it with a fitting similar to the one on the ECM temp sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||11-27-2000||05:48 PM||||Mine is a manual 4 speed, if i'm looking at the right thing, mine is on the drivers side sitting straight up and down into the drive-axel, is this the correct thing, if so how hard is it to replace, it has the same connections you where talking about, thanks..jim||||reg||5
Z||000003||StuGood||11-28-2000||04:19 PM||||Think you got it (if it's the same as all my manual Fieros - but I don't own a 1984 model).<P>To replace it, unplug the wire, get a 10mm socket on an extension and loosen the bolt underneath.  Loosening the bolt allows a little metal tab to swing out of a slot in the side of the VSS.  Then, carefully pull the VSS straight up out of the transaxle.  Make sure its plastic gear doesn't fall off, into the trans. ||||reg||1
